    "section": "TEMPLATE CHECK — journal class, but not a gate",
    "text": "TEMPLATE CHECK: note whether the manuscript was written with the JOURNAL TEMPLATE — i.e. it uses the\njournal class (`\\documentclass{artaquest}` or `artaquest.cls`). Set `template_ok` explicitly — `true` if it\nuses the journal class, `false` if not — and never omit it (an omitted value defaults to template-OK). If it is\nNOT the journal template, that is NOT a reason to reject (any compiling LaTeX is accepted) — but you MUST\nWARN the author in your `report`: recommend they use the <journal name> LaTeX template\n(https://artaquest.com/papers/artaquest-latex-template.zip) for consistent formatting + metadata next time.",
    "why": "The reviewer notes whether the manuscript used the journal's LaTeX class and sets template_ok explicitly (true/false, never omitted — an omitted value would silently default to template-OK). Importantly, NOT using the template is never a reason to reject — any compiling LaTeX is accepted — but the reviewer must warn the author and point them to the template (the <journal name> placeholder is filled with the actual journal) for consistent formatting and metadata next time. This keeps the journal welcoming to outside submissions while nudging toward house style."
