    "text": "FINALLY, write your verdict as STRICT JSON to this EXACT absolute path (not a relative path, even if\nyou have cd'd elsewhere): <workdir>/verdict.json\nwith this shape and nothing else in the file:\n  {\"reproduced\": true|false, \"verdict\": \"accept\"|\"revise\"|\"reject\", \"score\": 0-100,\n   \"scores\": {\"reproducibility\":0-100,\"honesty\":0-100,\"communication\":0-100,\"visualisation\":0-100,\"accessibility\":0-100,\"references\":0-100,\"significance\":0-100},\n   \"template_ok\": true|false,  // true iff the manuscript used the journal class (artaquest.cls)\n   \"report\": \"Constructive Markdown review aimed at maximising the paper's outreach. Structure it: **What works** (genuine strengths); **Reproduction** (what you ran, what reproduced, exact commands/errors); **To strengthen the paper for reach** (specific, actionable suggestions on communication, figures/visualisation, accessibility, framing — a sharper title, a clearer abstract line, a better figure, a plain-language takeaway); **Verdict rationale**. Be a generous expert mentor: precise, encouraging, never dismissive.\",\n   \"repro\": [\"ordered shell commands that reproduce from a blank machine — a fallback used to build the notebook if needed; include only on accept\"]}\nThe `report` is published verbatim to the author and the public, so make it specific and constructive.\nWriting the verdict file is the LAST thing you do — it is how your review is recorded.",
    "why": "The strict JSON the reviewer writes last (to the placeholder <workdir>/verdict.json) — it is how the review is recorded and posted back to the platform. It carries reproduced (true/false), the verdict, the overall score, the seven per-axis sub-scores in the `scores` object (these are what render as the transparent per-axis rubric breakdown on each published review round), template_ok, the published Markdown report (structured: what works, reproduction, how to strengthen, rationale), and the repro shell steps used as a fallback to build the notebook. The report is published verbatim, so it must be specific and constructive; writing this file is the final action of the review."
